## Commits
### afca9ee
chore(core): switch the coverage gate on

Node reads node.config.json only with
--experimental-default-config-file, so until now the minimums in that
file were inert and a coverage run below them exited 0. The coverage
script now passes the flag, and a run that misses any minimum exits 1.

The lcov reporter does not print test diagnostics, so with it alone the
threshold error was invisible even though the exit code was 1. A second
spec reporter on stdout prints that line; the lcov reporter and its
destination are unchanged.

CI runs the coverage script as a step of the test job on every matrix
version, after the plain test step, so a pull request or trunk push that
drops coverage fails on each runtime.

The tests docs heading now uses the glossary term "coverage gate" and
states that the script exits non-zero below any minimum.


